{
  "explanation": "An attacker successfully authenticated to the system via SSH using compromised administrative credentials from a suspicious IP address. Following the login, the attacker escalated privileges by creating a new backdoor user account with root UID/GID 0 disguised as a system utility and inspected existing scheduled tasks. This indicates full system compromise and persistent unauthorized access.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Persistence",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Immediately isolate the compromised host (web-01) from the network to prevent further malicious activity.",
    "Revoke and rotate all administrative credentials, and terminate active SSH sessions for the affected user.",
    "Audit system accounts, cron jobs, and sudoers configurations to remove any unauthorized backdoors or persistent access mechanisms."
  ]
}
